From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 06:38:22 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: remove the per-port network device driver

The four front-panel sockets of the first switch macro, and the fifth of
the second on the boards that have one, are switch ports. They are
described and driven as such now: a switch driver owns the macro, a
tagging driver reads the port a frame arrived on out of the header the
packet MAC prepends, and one conduit network device carries the
processor's end of each macro's datapath. Nothing binds this driver's
device tree node any more.

What it did beyond that is gone with it. The transmit path built the
packet MAC header by hand, which the tagging driver does; the receive
accounting belonged to network devices that no longer exist; and the
bring-up sequence allocated its dequeue resources through the datapath
registry, which the buffer manager now does at probe for every port the
device tree describes.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

